# Generated harbor task datasets. These default OUTSIDE the repo (see the
# minds-evals-generate recipe) because each embeds a full mngr-internal clone;
# this ignore is a safety net for anyone who points --output back in-tree.
datasets/
# The input data the checked-in eval configs upload, which the safety net above would otherwise
# swallow: a step's `files.source` is resolved relative to the config file, so this path is fixed.
!configs/datasets/
# Local harbor job results (the run recipe points -o here).
jobs/
# Single-trial regrades (`harbor trial regrade -o` points here). Its output is a bare trial
# directory with no job config.json, so it does not belong under jobs/, which `harbor view` reads
# as a folder of jobs.
regrades/
# Per-user local secrets (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY etc.), sourced by dev runs only.
.env.local
# The vendored viewer's toolchain and build output, both produced by scripts/build_viewer.sh.
# bun lives inside the project rather than on the developer's machine, since only the viewer
# recipes need it.
.bun/
viewer/node_modules/
viewer/build/
# The repo root ignores **/lib/ as Python build output. The vendored viewer has a real source
# directory at that path, and the negation has to name the directory itself: git never descends
# into an excluded directory, so a pattern matching only the files inside it would not bring them
# back.
!viewer/app/lib/
